The Penal Code, in this Order referred to as the Code, is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after section 380A - causing disruption to key service 380B. (1) Whoever commits theft which causes, or which he knows is likely to cause, a disruption to the provision of any key service shall be with imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 10 years and whipping with not less than 4 strokes and not more than 12 strokes.

(2) which section 258 of the Criminal Procedure 7) applies, the Court shall sentence the offender, instead of whipping, to imprisonment for a term which may extend to 12 months, in to the punishment to which he has been sentenced under this

(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), "key service" means any of the following services - {a} a service directly related to the provision to the general public of water, sewerage, drainage, gas, electricity, waste and telecommunications and other forms of mass media communication (including radio and television services); {b} and rescue service, a fire-fighting service, a service providing rapid response to requests for help in a medical or other health emergency service;

(c) a service directly related to the provision to the general or healtl1care services at a hospital, healthcare or other like institution;

(d) a service that is critical to ensuring the reliable supply in Brunei Darussalam of food which is safe and suitable for human consun1ption;.

(e) a service directly related to ensuring the provision to the general public of reliable and safe public transport by land, water or air within Brunei Darussalam or to and from Brunei Darussalam; If! a payments clearing and settlement service for payment or securities, a service directly related to the provision to the general public of banking facilities and financial services associated with banking business, a securities trading, clearing and settlement service, and any other like service that is necessary to the financial market or financial institutions in Brunei Darussalam or the disruption of which would have a widespread adverse effect on the financial system in Brunei Darussalam or the economy of Brunei Darussalam, or both; (g} any other service that is critical to maintaining public health, the social and economic stability of Brunei Darussalam or its people, or its national security.". of section 411
